Hi Carlos,

> considerations of the different class systems

Based on how data can be incorrect and the way we are validating variables, we should use S3. S4 is too restrictive because it does not allow for incorrect data types during object creation. Since we are only checking for errors after the data is added, we need a system that allows "bad" data to exist in our data frame temporarily so it can be validated. If we were validating data before adding it to the data frame, S4’s strict enforcement of data types would be a better fit

> an be reimagine in an object oriented design fashion

As previously mentioned, only the gitlog and gitlog_entities tables are suitable for inheritance. I do not see a practical use for inheritance in the edge and node structures, as the parameters vary significantly across different graphs. The only likely changes would be the previously mentioned name updates to the project_dependencies_edgelist.

