### From what I can tell these would be the objects.

``` r
// Generic
base <- function(x, ...) {
  UseMethod("base")
}

// Default 
base.default <- function(ane, ad, ch, cne, cd, nlc, cs, ...) {
  value <- list(
    author_name_email = ane, 
    author_datetimetz = ad, 
    commit_hash = ch, 
    committer_name_email = cne,  
    committer_datetimetz = cd, 
    n_lines_changed = nlc, 
    commit_summary = cs
  )
  class(value) <- "base"
  value
}

// Project Git Method
base.project_git <- function(input_list, fp, fpr, ...) {
  value <- list(
    file_pathname = fp, 
    file_pathname_renamed = fpr,
    original_data = input_list
  )
  class(value) <- "project_git" 
  value
}

// Identity Method
base.identity <- function(x, id, rn, ...) {
  // Runs base.project_git first and gets that list
  value <- NextMethod()
  // Add to the list
  value$identity_id <- id
  value$raw_name    <- rn
  // Update the class chain
  class(value) <- c("identity", "project_git", "base")
  return(value)
}
```

Hi Carlos,

With all the columns in the gitlog module I think taking a step back and doing just the nodes for the three notebooks is better.

